{
  "an6.45:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 6.45 ",
  "an6.45:0.2": "5. About Dhammika ",
  "an6.45:0.3": "Debt ",
  "an6.45:1.1": "“Mendicants, isn’t poverty suffering in the world for a person who enjoys sensual pleasures?” ",
  "an6.45:1.2": "“Yes, sir.” ",
  "an6.45:2.1": "“When a poor, penniless person falls into debt, isn’t being in debt also suffering in the world for a person who enjoys sensual pleasures?” ",
  "an6.45:2.2": "“Yes, sir.” ",
  "an6.45:3.1": "“When a poor person who has fallen into debt agrees to pay interest, isn’t the interest also suffering in the world for a person who enjoys sensual pleasures?” ",
  "an6.45:3.2": "“Yes, sir.” ",
  "an6.45:4.1": "“When a poor person who has fallen into debt and agreed to pay interest fails to pay it when it falls due, they get a warning. ",
  "an6.45:4.2": "Isn’t being warned suffering in the world for a person who enjoys sensual pleasures?” ",
  "an6.45:4.3": "“Yes, sir.” ",
  "an6.45:5.1": "“When a poor person fails to pay after getting a warning, they’re prosecuted. ",
  "an6.45:5.2": "Isn’t being prosecuted suffering in the world for a person who enjoys sensual pleasures?” ",
  "an6.45:5.3": "“Yes, sir.” ",
  "an6.45:6.1": "“When a poor person fails to pay after being prosecuted, they’re imprisoned. ",
  "an6.45:6.2": "Isn’t being imprisoned suffering in the world for a person who enjoys sensual pleasures?” ",
  "an6.45:6.3": "“Yes, sir.” ",
  "an6.45:7.1": "“So mendicants, poverty, debt